  "cil_liability": true,
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposed development, by reason of the poor outlook to the units of block B on the northern elevation facing the rear service road and interrelationship with Block A, compromised daylight and sunlight to private amenity spaces and internal living spaces of flats B1 and B3, poor siting, insufficient and cramped refuse store, poor access and failure to demonstrate the provision of a wheelchair Accessible Unit for block B, would result in poor quality accommodation which would not be fit for purpose, to the detriment of the residential amenities of the future occupiers,&amp;nbsp; contrary to the National Planning Policy Framework (2024), Policies D3 (7), D5, D7 and D6 of the London Plan (2021), and Policies GR1, GR3A, HO2, of the Harrow&amp;nbsp; Local Plan (2021 - 2041).",
    "&lt;p class=&quot;MsoListParagraph&quot; style=&quot;margin-left: 23.4pt;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; The\r\nproposal, by reason of failure to provide 35 per cent&amp;nbsp; family sized units with 3 or more bedrooms\r\nincluding the provision of no family units on the ground floor of block B and\r\nthe overall high proportion of smaller units below 4 persons, would result in\r\nan inappropriate and inadequate housing mix, having regard to the location of\r\nthe site and the character of its surroundings as well as the evidence of local\r\nneed which identifies the need for more larger family sized units, and would\r\nfail to create inclusive and mixed communities, contrary to the provisions of\r\nthe National Planning Policy Framework (2024), policy H10 of the London Plan\r\n(2021) and policies HO1 and HO2 of the Harrow Local Plan (2021-2041).&lt;font face=&quot;Arial, sans-serif&quot;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p class=&quot;MsoListParagraph&quot; style=&quot;margin-left:23.4pt;mso-add-space:auto;\r\ntext-align:justify;text-indent:-18.0pt;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1;mso-prop-change:\r\n&amp;quot;Nicola Rankin&amp;quot; 20260422T1712&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:&amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;,sans-serif;mso-fareast-font-family:&amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;&quot;&gt;The\r\nproposed development by reason of failure to provide the maximum reasonable\r\nlevel of affordable housing and insufficient justification to demonstrate why\r\nsuch provision cannot be delivered would fail to contribute to mixed and\r\nbalanced communities and meet local housing need, contrary to the National\r\nPlanning Policy Framework (2024), policy H4 of The London Plan (2021) and\r\npolicy HO4 of the Harrow Local Plan (2021-2041)&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:11.0pt;line-height:107%;\r\nfont-family:&amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;,sans-serif;mso-fareast-font-family:&amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;;\r\nmso-ansi-language:EN-GB;mso-fareast-language:EN-US;mso-bidi-language:AR-SA&quot;&gt;The\r\nproposed development, in the absence of a sufficient Noise Impact Assessment\r\nand Odour Assessment, has failed to demonstrate that the future occupiers of\r\nthe proposed development would not be adversely affected in terms of noise and\r\nodour, resulting in poor quality living conditions, to the detriment of their residential\r\namenities, contrary to the National Planning Policy Framework (2024), Policies\r\nD3 (7), D6 and D14 &amp;nbsp;of the London Plan\r\n(2021), and Policies GR1 and HO2, of the Harrow&amp;nbsp;\r\nLocal Plan (2021 - 2041).&lt;/span&gt;"
  ],
